    {
      "section": "time.clock",
      "confidence": "medium",
      "note": "'tuku {h}' (tuku = o'clock strike), 'tuku {h} ho balun' for half, and 'tuku {h} ho minutu <N>' counting up with Tetum numerals (numeral after noun, as in the locale's 'minutu {n}'). Portuguese-style 'menus kuartu' subtraction exists in Tetun Prasa but was not used because I could not verify it; the counting-up form is safe but may feel long at :45."
